Author: Buu <buddingnewinsights@gmail.com>
Date:   Tue Aug 25 11:55:59 2026 +0700

    feat(solid): transitionMs/transitionEasing props animate style changes (S12c)
    
    Declarative API matching the placeholder/minRows prop pattern: set
    transitionMs (optionally transitionEasing) on an element, then future style
    changes DIFF against the last-sent bag — numeric animatable keys that
    changed emit one setAnimation (helper interpolates); everything else flows
    in the companion setStyle, which omits the animated keys so it does not
    snap them to the target before interpolation starts. First style set (no
    previous) is static, like CSS transitions. No transitionMs → plain
    setStyle, unchanged behavior.
    
    Export ANIMATABLE_STYLE_KEYS/EASING_NAMES from @solid-gpui/protocol.
    
    Tests: animated keys excluded from the companion setStyle; no-transition
    stays plain; non-animatable/non-numeric changes stay static.
    
    bun 82/82, tsc x3.

